  "metalHelp1": "Open the tool away from metal. That first reading counts as “no metal”.",
  "metalHelp2": "Move the phone slowly over the area. The sensor is usually near the top of the phone. It beeps faster the closer you get to metal; tap the speaker to mute.",
  "metalHelp3": "“Metal nearby” means a small change, “Metal detected” a strong one. Like the game of hot and cold, the screen warms from cool blue to glowing red as you get closer, and the phone buzzes on a find if vibration is on.",
  "metalHelp4": "Hold the phone still for a few seconds and it re-zeroes itself, so a false reading fades away. To check a spot again, move the phone away and back. Tap Set baseline to re-zero at once.",
  "metalTip": "It only senses iron, steel and magnets, not aluminium, copper, gold or silver. Magnetic phone cases affect it.",
